# Keep the host's build output OUT of the image.
#
# "COPY . ." would otherwise ship every object, kernel image and - the one
# that actually breaks the build - every gcc-generated .d dependency file
# from the developer's own tree into the container. Those .d files name
# host absolute paths for toolchain headers:
#
#   build/proc.o: source/proc.c /usr/arm-linux-gnueabihf/include/stdc-predef.h ...
#
# and a path that does not exist inside the image, with no rule to make it,
# is a hard error rather than a rebuild:
#
#   make[1]: *** No rule to make target
#     '/usr/arm-linux-gnueabihf/include/stdc-predef.h', needed by 'build/proc.o'
#
# This was latent for a long time and was being masked: the eight ports whose
# test-xv6.py used to run "make clean" first wiped the stale artifacts inside
# the container before anything read them. Dropping that clean (so "make
# test-all" could reuse "make build-all") exposed it. The Makefiles now also
# pass "-MP" alongside "-MD", which emits a phony target per header so a
# vanished header is a rebuild rather than an error - that is the general fix
# and it covers a renamed/deleted header locally too. This file is the other
# half: a container build should compile from SOURCE, not inherit whatever
# the host happened to leave lying around, which also keeps the build context
# small and the image reproducible.
#
# Mirrors the repo's own .gitignore patterns - keep the two in step.

.git
Makefile.config

# Object files, dependency files, archives, and linker/debug byproducts.
# None of these are tracked in git (verified: "git ls-files | grep -E
# '\.(o|d|a|elf|asm|sym|map|dis)$'" is empty), so excluding them wholesale
# is safe.
**/*.o
**/*.d
**/*.a
**/*.elf
**/*.asm
**/*.sym
**/*.map
**/*.dis

# Per-port object directories.
**/build/
**/build-qemu/
**/out/

# Generated kernel/filesystem images. Unlike the extensions above, a few
# .bin files ARE checked in - the font bitmap tables several Pi ports
# .incbin into the kernel - so those are negated back in below; order
# matters here, later patterns win.
#
# No source/fs.img is negated: every port that embeds a filesystem image now
# GENERATES it from its own uprogs/ during the build (arm-pi1, arm-pi2 and
# arm-pi3 all have a "source/fs.img: uprogs-fs-img" rule), so shipping a
# host-built copy into the container would be the same stale-artifact
# mistake this file exists to prevent.
**/*.img
**/*.bin
# claude: negated by NAME rather than by full path. These used to be seven
# explicit paths (forks/arm-pi1/source/font.bin and friends), and Phase 0's
# layout move renamed source/ to kernel/ underneath them - so the negations
# silently stopped matching, the fonts were excluded from the build context,
# and the container build failed where the host build passed:
#
#   kernel/entry.s:19: Error: file not found: font1.bin
#
# Every .bin file tracked in this repo is one of these font bitmap tables
# (verified: "git ls-files | grep '\.bin$'" lists nothing else), so matching
# on the basename is both correct and immune to the three remaining Pi ports'
# layout moves.
!**/font.bin
!**/font1.bin

# Other build outputs named in .gitignore: compiled user programs (xv6's
# "_name" convention), the generated trap-vector table, boot sector,
# secondary-CPU trampoline, the memfs kernel variant, and mkfs itself.
**/_*
**/vectors.S
**/bootblock
**/entryother
**/kernelmemfs
# claude: was "**/mkfs/mkfs". Phase 0 moved every port's mkfs.c into tools/,
# so no fork has an mkfs/ directory any more and that pattern matched
# nothing - meaning a host-built mkfs binary would have been copied into the
# image, exactly the stale-artifact leak this file exists to prevent. No
# tracked file in the repo is named "mkfs" (they are all mkfs.c), so
# excluding the bare name anywhere is safe and does not need updating when a
# port's build directory changes again.
**/mkfs
**/.gdbinit

# Editor and tooling leftovers.
**/*~
**/__pycache__/
